 "narrative": "**SCALECRAFT SOCIAL SNAPSHOT — @talon__wilson**\n\n**WHERE YOU STAND**\nYour account holds a strong baseline score of 84 out of 100, with a low Posting Consistency score of 73 driving most of the gap due to publishing 1.9 times per week against a target of 4 to 5 posts. What is already working exceptionally well is your ability to blend breathtaking Pacific Northwest imagery with deeply reflective, poetic caption storytelling, driving an extraordinary 58.65% average engagement rate.\n\n**THE SINGLE BIGGEST OPPORTUNITY**\nYour single highest-leverage opportunity is to land paid brand partnerships and sponsor deals by adding a direct business contact line, curated Story Highlights, and a strategic link-in-bio destination (such as a media kit or preset/itinerary link). Your September 17, 2026 Cape Flattery Reel pulled 44,075 views and 8,627 engagements, but without a clear media kit link or contact bio line, high-intent brand managers exit without sending inquiries or booking sponsorships.\n\n**YOUR 30-60-90 DAY PATH**\n\n1. **Days 1–30 – Consistency & Brand Readiness:** Update your bio to read \"Pacific Northwest imagery & reflective stories. Inquiries: [add your direct business email]\" and set a schedule to post 2 voiceover Reels per week on Thursdays and Saturdays using recycled b-roll from your video archive. Thursday is your highest-performing day (averaging 3,051 engagements), and establishing a predictable 2-post weekly cadence from home closes your posting gap without requiring new shooting trips.\n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + your weeks 1–4 posting calendar\n\n2. **Days 31–60 – Proof & Grid Highlights:** Pin your top-performing September 17 Cape Flattery Reel (44,075 views) to the top of your grid and build a dedicated \"Brand Work\" Story Highlight using existing b-roll and voiceovers detailing your gear setup and past brand features. Pinning your best post (which hit 8.76x your account average engagement) gives visiting brand managers immediate proof of your viral reach and aesthetic quality.\n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + your weeks 5–8 posting calendar\n\n3. **Days 61–90 – Conversion & Pitch Infrastructure:** Place a free link-in-bio page containing a downloadable media kit PDF and an email list sign-up for photography presets or PNW travel itineraries. Converting your top-of-funnel Reel audience (which averages 1,336 engagements per post) into an owned email list and accessible rate sheet gives brands a frictionless path to hire you before spring shoots begin.\n   🔒 4 more moves for this phase + your weeks 9–12 posting calendar\n\n**WHAT YOUR BEST POSTS HAVE IN COMMON**\nYour top post was the September 17, 2026 Reel at Cape Flattery, which achieved 8.76x your account average engagement. Your top three posts all feature high-contrast outdoor landscapes paired with voiceover narrative and captions that open with a strong reflective line (\"The last few steps in America...\", \"Normalizing black faces...\"). In contrast, your bottom three posts rely on generic captions (\"I don’t see why people wait to live...\") and lack a distinct narrative hook, resulting in engagement far below your 985-engagement average.\n\n**WHAT THE FULL PLAN ADDS**\nThe full plan includes the remaining 12 moves across all three phases, your complete 12-week posting calendar tailored to archive content, and custom voiceover prompts written directly from your best-performing posts.",
